      "body": "## Overview\r\n\r\nUse the preallocated maximum C128 sparse width in batch-invariant mode, so metadata and workspace shapes do not follow the longest request in the current batch. Keep adaptive width outside BI mode. During block-size-8 graph capture, discard the C128 boundary flag in both modes to keep replay state stable.\r\n\r\n## Test\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nuv run --no-project python -m pytest --confcutdir=tests/kernels \\\r\n    tests/kernels/attention/test_flashmla_sparse.py::test_c128a_batch_invariant_metadata_uses_fixed_width \\\r\n    tests/kernels/test_compressor_kv_cache.py::test_compressor_graph_capture_discards_c128_boundary -q\r\n```\r\n\r\nH100: **4 passed**. The composed P2 integration branch reported **34 passed, 9 skipped** in `test_flashmla_sparse.py`. End-to-end model evaluation remains unrun.\r\n\r\nH20: **4 targeted cases passed** on this PR head.\r\n",
